If you prefer to put it that way.

00:33:24.180 --> 00:33:25.740
Well, I've had enough of that kind of talk today,

00:33:25.740 --> 00:33:26.920
and I'm tired of it.

00:33:35.850 --> 00:33:38.230
- This yours? - Yes.

00:33:38.230 --> 00:33:39.910
- Then you admit it.

00:33:39.910 --> 00:33:42.910
Perhaps you'll admit throwing it on the roof outside of Kester's room.

00:33:42.910 --> 00:33:44.430
- No, I didn't.

00:33:44.430 --> 00:33:47.220
It's been missing from my dresser for two days.

00:33:47.220 --> 00:33:50.480
- Did you report that to anybody? - No.

00:33:50.480 --> 00:33:52.050
- Well, that's all now.

00:33:52.050 --> 00:33:54.150
Well, I'd check up with that lawyer of yours.

00:33:54.150 --> 00:33:55.890
Don't you try to make a getaway again.

00:34:01.850 --> 00:34:09.350
Oh, Mr. Hall, where did you get such an unusual knife as this?

00:34:09.840 --> 00:34:10.910
In Mexico.

00:34:13.730 --> 00:34:18.960
I want to speak to Mr. Bertram F. Howell.

00:34:20.340 --> 00:34:22.060
Never mind who it is, I want to talk to him.

00:34:24.270 --> 00:34:25.610
Oh, you know where he can be reached?

00:34:27.710 --> 00:34:28.320
Thank you.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.000
Hall's lying too.

00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:33.410
House been up in Maine for a week.

00:34:33.410 --> 00:34:34.410
He's not expected back until tomorrow.

00:34:34.410 --> 00:34:36.410
Well, I think Hall took a long chance and missed.

00:34:36.410 --> 00:34:37.410
Oh, you thinking again?

00:34:37.410 --> 00:34:38.410
It's mighty smart of him.

00:34:38.410 --> 00:34:40.410
Well, I suppose you know who killed Kester.

00:34:40.410 --> 00:34:42.410
Certainly I do, but I've got to prove it.

00:34:42.410 --> 00:34:43.330
Where's that lawyer and the secretary?

00:34:43.330 --> 00:34:46.250
Up in Kester's room, looking over his stuff.

00:34:46.250 --> 00:34:55.200
Anything missing?

00:34:55.200 --> 00:34:58.520
Can't find anything out of the way regarding his investments.

00:34:58.520 --> 00:35:00.000
Of course, uh...

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.420
I can't be sure till I get back to town and check his deposit box.

00:35:02.420 --> 00:35:04.040
You fellas were pretty close to Kester.

00:35:04.040 --> 00:35:05.260
Ever hear him mention Hall?

00:35:05.260 --> 00:35:08.930
I've never heard his name mentioned in the ten years I was associated with Mr. Kester.

00:35:08.930 --> 00:35:11.610
Just an idea of my own, of course, but on one or two occasions,

00:35:11.610 --> 00:35:14.250
I heard Mr. Hall mention the Arco Mining Company.

00:35:14.250 --> 00:35:16.810
And Mr. Kester seemed well uncomfortable.

00:35:16.810 --> 00:35:18.750
Kester owned some of that stock, didn't he?

00:35:18.750 --> 00:35:20.030
He did until the day before yesterday.

00:35:20.030 --> 00:35:23.470
I sold the last of it for him, $14,000 worth.

00:35:23.470 --> 00:35:25.030
It's ended here in this little black book.

00:35:30.440 --> 00:35:32.100
Did Hall have any visitors since he's been here?

00:35:32.320 --> 00:35:33.740
No, sir. Make any phone calls?

00:35:33.970 --> 00:35:35.570
Not that I know of. Did he write any letters?

00:35:36.280 --> 00:35:38.170
Yes, sir, he did. A few days ago

00:35:38.170 --> 00:35:39.940
he rang for me, handed me a letter

00:35:39.940 --> 00:35:41.560
and asked me to have it sent

00:35:41.560 --> 00:35:43.960
registered special delivery. Did you notice who too?

00:35:44.330 --> 00:35:45.800
I did, sir. Seeing as

00:35:45.800 --> 00:35:47.600
how he wanted it registered, to a

00:35:47.600 --> 00:35:50.100
Mr. Hall, sir. Did he say anything

00:35:50.100 --> 00:35:51.850
else? Well, he asked me if

00:35:51.850 --> 00:35:53.730
Miss Kester was up yet. I said no.

00:35:54.300 --> 00:35:55.760
Then he asked me to send Dora to him.

00:35:55.960 --> 00:35:57.260
And did you? Yes, sir.

00:35:58.040 --> 00:36:00.000
First she lies for the girl, then she hides

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:16.430
the money and now she's in cahoots for this fellow haul. When did Miss Kester give you

00:36:16.430 --> 00:36:21.840
that $1,200 to hide for? What $1,200? The $1,200 was found in your knitting ball. Come on.

00:36:22.150 --> 00:36:27.340
You know what I mean. I swear with the holy mother of... I haven't any idea how that $1,200

00:36:27.340 --> 00:36:30.000
got in my knitting ball. I must say it's

00:36:30.280 --> 00:36:34.680
business to be playing tricks and hiding twelve hundred dollars in my knitting ball stop saying

00:36:34.680 --> 00:36:38.810
twelve hundred dollars in your knitting ball yes sir do you know anything about this fellow hall

00:36:38.810 --> 00:36:44.500
he's a very fine gentleman and very generous too annie the second maid was telling me he gave her

00:36:44.500 --> 00:36:51.160
a dollar he said just because she was so pretty but never a bit familiar just kind and generous

00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:58.220
ever hear catch to talk about him never a word you ever see him before never set eyes on him

00:36:58.220 --> 00:37:00.000
then what does he want with you in his room yet

00:37:00.030 --> 00:37:02.430
Lennox was allowing his room to be neglected.

00:37:02.430 --> 00:37:05.580
Only one washcloth, and a broken curtain sash,

00:37:05.580 --> 00:37:07.640
and the dust was three inches thick.

00:37:07.640 --> 00:37:08.900
You should have seen it.

00:37:08.900 --> 00:37:11.000
- Why did you tell me Miss Kester went directly downstairs

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:12.900
when you knew she went to her grandfather's room?

00:37:12.900 --> 00:37:13.860
- She didn't.

00:37:13.860 --> 00:37:15.950
I saw her go downstairs.

00:37:15.950 --> 00:37:18.260
- Mrs. Pritchard told me she saw her come out of that room.

00:37:18.260 --> 00:37:20.540
- If you want to believe her, go ahead.

00:37:20.540 --> 00:37:22.080
Five years I've known her,

00:37:22.080 --> 00:37:25.480
never a word of trust could I put in her.

00:37:25.480 --> 00:37:26.380
- Thank you.

00:37:26.380 --> 00:37:30.000
- She's great, tremendous.

00:37:30.320 --> 00:37:32.240
I'd take my hat off to her if I had a hat on.

00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:34.290
She's a marvelous liar, if that's what you mean.

00:37:34.550 --> 00:37:35.950
It looks to me like a murder syndicate.

00:37:36.390 --> 00:37:38.090
Miss Kester, Miller, Hall, and Dora.

00:37:38.580 --> 00:37:40.170
All of them know something they're not telling.

00:37:40.820 --> 00:37:42.280
And their lies don't hang together.

00:37:46.860 --> 00:37:49.060
There's something I should have told you about a while ago,

00:37:49.200 --> 00:37:51.760
but he was such a decent fellow that I hated to believe it of him.

00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:52.280
What is it?

00:37:52.530 --> 00:37:52.850
This.

00:37:53.910 --> 00:37:56.270
I saw it fall out of Hall's pocket right after lunch.

00:37:57.510 --> 00:37:57.970
Thank you.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.960
Thank you very much.

00:38:00.960 --> 00:38:03.760
Blood?

00:38:03.760 --> 00:38:04.760
Of course it is.

00:38:04.760 --> 00:38:05.760
Oh, you'll find it's his own.

00:38:05.760 --> 00:38:08.870
I was walking around the house with Hall this morning and he got a nosebleed.

00:38:08.870 --> 00:38:11.970
That guy hasn't got blood enough to get a nosebleed.

00:41:14.110 --> 00:41:16.810
- I'm awfully sorry. - Oh, you frighten me.

00:41:16.810 --> 00:41:20.270
I was on my way to the kitchen, saw the door open, and thought it rather unusual.

00:41:20.270 --> 00:41:23.700
Yes. Yes, two minds with but a single thought.

00:41:23.700 --> 00:41:27.370
You know, I too was hunting the icebox, and I lost my way.

00:41:27.370 --> 00:41:30.000
It can't be down here. Suppose we look together.

00:41:33.320 --> 00:41:49.140
- It's right over here.

00:41:49.140 --> 00:41:51.660
- Well, Glatton, save some rice pudding for me.

00:42:01.560 --> 00:42:03.690
I was so famous I couldn't sleep.

00:42:03.690 --> 00:42:08.100
Cold nothing. I've been thinking of this all evening.

00:42:08.100 --> 00:42:11.360
It's one dish I couldn't relish in a house of murder.

00:42:11.360 --> 00:42:18.390
Mmm, this is what I like, informality.

00:42:18.390 --> 00:42:22.390
Wouldn't the papers like to get a picture of us sitting around in our sleepers?

00:42:22.390 --> 00:42:24.600
Goodness knows what my husband would think.

00:42:24.600 --> 00:42:29.160
Please don't mention our meeting tonight, even though it was accidental.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:32.580
- Don't worry on my account, madam.

00:42:32.580 --> 00:42:35.680
- Well, you speak for yourself.

00:42:35.680 --> 00:42:39.230
- Don't worry, I won't tell you.

00:42:39.230 --> 00:42:41.930
- Human nature's a funny thing, isn't it?

00:42:41.930 --> 00:42:44.770
Here we are, all under suspicion for murder,

00:42:44.770 --> 00:42:47.350
sitting around eating.

00:42:47.350 --> 00:42:51.010
We must have clear consciences, or none at all.

00:42:51.010 --> 00:42:53.690
- Your insinuation is unjustified, Mr. Tracy.

00:42:53.690 --> 00:42:56.180
My conscience is clear enough to resent that remark.

00:43:05.210 --> 00:43:09.770
- Just exactly, what do you know about this murder, Mr. Hall?

00:43:09.770 --> 00:43:18.720
- Just as much as you do, Mr. Tracy.

00:43:18.720 --> 00:43:20.200
- How do we know you didn't do it?

00:43:20.200 --> 00:43:23.020
- Well, for one thing, I wasn't mentioned in his will.

00:43:23.020 --> 00:43:27.290
- Come on, he never did me any dirt.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:33.960
didn't want his money and he hasn't anything on me. The only reason I might have had for

00:43:33.960 --> 00:43:40.750
killing him was that I didn't like him. He was a snob. That's a swell reason. Certainly. It's

00:43:40.750 --> 00:43:46.900
always a good reason for making away with anyone. Then I'm six feet tall, weigh 185 pounds, and

00:43:46.900 --> 00:43:52.680
belong to the Bombay Bicycle Club. Say, you're not throwing me off with a lot of that fresh gab.

00:43:53.090 --> 00:44:00.000
I was just thinking. What? I was just thinking somebody's liable to be bumped off anytime.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:06.030
now. How do you think of that? Well, when anybody starts suspecting the real murderer, they're

00:44:06.030 --> 00:44:13.310
gently quietly bumped off. Well, that gives me an idea. Maybe my life won't be so peaceful

00:44:13.310 --> 00:44:20.800
now. What do you know? Did it ever strike you that it was Mrs. Pritchett who opened the

00:44:20.800 --> 00:44:27.530
closet door and found Kester? Yet her fingerprints were not on that doorknob. Say, boy, you got

00:44:27.530 --> 00:44:29.860
something there. And another thing.

00:44:30.280 --> 00:44:33.520
Mrs. Pritchard was on that second floor during the last dance.

00:44:34.250 --> 00:44:35.410
Yeah, and so were you.

00:44:36.950 --> 00:44:38.570
I've got another idea.

00:44:40.890 --> 00:44:41.090
Hmm?

00:44:42.030 --> 00:44:42.640
Yep.

00:44:44.460 --> 00:44:49.250
You know, that little black book might tell a big story if it could only talk.

00:44:49.770 --> 00:44:50.930
Ah, you're a pain.

00:44:51.160 --> 00:44:53.280
You're always going in for little black books.

00:44:56.170 --> 00:44:58.130
Well, I told you somebody was going to get bumped off.

00:45:07.840 --> 00:45:08.680
- I don't know yet.

00:45:08.680 --> 00:45:09.500
Keep quiet.

00:45:09.500 --> 00:45:10.340
Where was it?

00:45:10.340 --> 00:45:11.110
Shut up everybody.

00:45:11.110 --> 00:45:11.940
That was a shot.

00:45:11.940 --> 00:45:27.260
Sounded like it came from over there.

00:45:27.260 --> 00:45:29.370
Wake up.

00:45:29.370 --> 00:45:30.000
- What's the matter?

00:45:32.840 --> 00:45:35.020
- Wake up! - Come on, wake up!

00:45:35.020 --> 00:45:39.090
- What's happened? - We heard a shot, and it sounds like it came from this room.

00:45:39.090 --> 00:45:40.110
Anyone been in here?

00:45:40.110 --> 00:45:42.960
- No. Where's my wife? - How do I know?

00:45:42.960 --> 00:45:46.320
- Who sleeps next door? - Mr. Hall.

00:46:23.390 --> 00:46:29.800
through his heart I'll be doggone that's exactly the way Hall felt about it what do you mean

00:46:30.250 --> 00:46:31.810
Well, that's what he said when he looked at Kester.

00:46:32.850 --> 00:46:34.750
See, I never did understand what he meant.

00:46:37.110 --> 00:46:38.270
Find the body in the bedroom.

00:46:39.190 --> 00:46:41.090
We left everything just as we found it last night.

00:46:41.230 --> 00:46:43.010
He probably knew we were closing in on him.

00:46:43.390 --> 00:46:44.590
And took the easiest way out.

00:46:45.170 --> 00:46:46.840
I've had a grudge against Kester for years.

00:46:46.980 --> 00:46:48.080
Oh, pardon the interruption.

00:46:49.330 --> 00:46:51.530
I don't think Hall killed Kester.

00:46:52.010 --> 00:46:53.700
And I don't think he committed suicide.

00:46:54.320 --> 00:46:55.340
All right, Smarty.

00:46:55.990 --> 00:46:56.690
Spell your theory.

00:46:57.540 --> 00:46:58.480
Well, I was just wondering.

00:46:59.120 --> 00:47:00.000
Why wasn't Pritchett away?

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:06.190
by that shot and why wasn't his wife in the room with it maybe he was doped right that's why I've

00:47:06.190 --> 00:47:11.020
been hanging on to these and I think your chemist will find that someone's been hitting the junk

00:47:11.020 --> 00:47:17.670
tell the butler I want to see him and get Nate Pitchett right

00:47:42.000 --> 00:47:50.860
go on funny i don't seem to be able to keep awake you had a glass of wine last

00:47:50.860 --> 00:47:54.950
night didn't you two glasses the wine doesn't usually affect me like this

00:47:54.950 --> 00:48:00.000
two glasses yes my wife didn't want hers so i drank them both when lennox brought the

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:01.020
wine up to the room.

00:48:01.080 --> 00:48:01.520
Who took it?

00:48:02.360 --> 00:48:03.140
Let me see.

00:48:03.440 --> 00:48:04.460
I think my wife did.

00:48:05.860 --> 00:48:06.600
What's that got to do

00:48:06.600 --> 00:48:07.640
with what happened last night?

00:48:08.080 --> 00:48:08.820
Oh, nothing, nothing.

00:48:08.920 --> 00:48:09.600
Just clearing up

00:48:09.600 --> 00:48:10.480
a few odds and ends.

00:48:11.340 --> 00:48:12.180
This suicide

00:48:12.180 --> 00:48:13.360
sort of settles things.

00:48:16.420 --> 00:48:17.460
That'll be all just now.

00:48:23.030 --> 00:48:23.850
Where was Mrs. Pritchard

00:48:23.850 --> 00:48:24.290
last night?

00:48:24.690 --> 00:48:25.630
Well, let me think.

00:48:26.010 --> 00:48:27.060
I don't know.

00:48:27.470 --> 00:48:28.830
I didn't take any nose hurt

00:48:28.830 --> 00:48:29.550
until after everything

00:48:29.550 --> 00:48:30.000
was over.

00:48:35.530 --> 00:48:36.530
Oh, Dora.

00:48:36.530 --> 00:48:39.410
Yes, sir?

00:48:39.410 --> 00:48:40.410
You heard that shot, I presume?

00:48:40.410 --> 00:48:41.590
I did that.

00:48:41.590 --> 00:48:43.630
And I was never so scared in me whole life.

00:48:43.630 --> 00:48:45.770
Do you remember seeing Mrs. Pritchett come out into the hall?

00:48:45.770 --> 00:48:48.060
No, sir, I didn't.

00:48:48.060 --> 00:48:50.060
When I left my room, she was still there.

00:48:50.060 --> 00:48:52.060
I don't remember when she left.

00:48:52.060 --> 00:48:53.200
Your room?

00:48:53.200 --> 00:48:54.830
Yes, sir.

00:48:54.830 --> 00:48:55.830
What was she doing there?

00:48:55.830 --> 00:48:56.980
She was sleeping.

00:48:56.980 --> 00:49:00.000
She came in and walked me out of a sound sleep, saying as how nervous I was.

00:49:00.030 --> 00:49:03.070
and scared she was and wanted to sleep on the day couch.

00:49:03.070 --> 00:49:04.800
- Is she in the habit of doing that?

00:49:04.800 --> 00:49:07.170
- Not in the five years that I've known her,

00:49:07.170 --> 00:49:09.850
which if you ask me is five years too long.

00:49:09.850 --> 00:49:24.690
- Thank you.

00:49:24.690 --> 00:49:27.810
Captain, I realize you want me to stick around here

00:49:27.810 --> 00:49:30.000
'til this business is over, but I'd like to go

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:36.590
If you don't mind. Oh, I promise I'll be back this afternoon and I couldn't get away if I wanted to you all know me

00:49:36.950 --> 00:49:40.370
You know where he was last night when the shot was fired. Yeah, he was with me

00:49:40.610 --> 00:49:51.350
All right, then you can go thanks, but listen no funny business for the tail on that guy

00:49:51.350 --> 00:50:00.000
I sure would like to pin something on him now. Don't tell me you saved enough money to buy Arco mining stuff

00:50:00.250 --> 00:50:03.510
No, no. Tell me what you know about this company.

00:50:03.510 --> 00:50:05.570
Well, the Arco mine is in Mexico.

00:50:05.570 --> 00:50:11.060
It was developed under a partnership between Stephen Kester and a fellow named Roger Hall.

00:50:11.060 --> 00:50:14.110
And back in 1914, Kester froze the other fellow out.

00:50:14.110 --> 00:50:18.820
Unloaded his stock, washed the prices down, and left Hall holding the sack.

00:50:18.820 --> 00:50:22.690
Since that time, he's bought a lot of that stock back.

00:50:22.690 --> 00:50:25.430
And now it's one of the most valuable stocks on the market.

00:50:25.430 --> 00:50:27.350
How much stock did Kester hold?

00:50:27.350 --> 00:50:30.000
Well, you'll have to see the bank he did business with to find that out.

00:50:30.220 --> 00:50:34.860
All right. All right. Suppose you use your influence with that banker and call him up and have him have all the information when I get there.

00:50:35.020 --> 00:50:35.560
I'm in a hurry.

00:50:43.180 --> 00:50:47.520
He had one hundred and eleven thousand dollars worth two days before he was murdered.

00:50:47.840 --> 00:50:49.020
One hundred and eleven thousand?

00:50:49.020 --> 00:50:49.780
Mm-hmm.

00:51:01.630 --> 00:51:07.920
- Thanks.

00:51:07.920 --> 00:51:12.920
- In my opinion, the original figure was 111,000.

00:51:12.920 --> 00:51:16.610
The first one has been incorporated into a dollar sign,

00:51:16.610 --> 00:51:19.260
and the cross on the four has been added

00:51:19.260 --> 00:51:25.500
with an ink of a different chemical basis.

00:51:25.500 --> 00:51:30.000
- Could have been very easy, couldn't it?

00:51:41.260 --> 00:51:42.860
Well, here I am again. Where's everybody?

00:51:43.270 --> 00:51:43.710
In there.

00:51:48.570 --> 00:51:51.750
Then, uh, Mr. Hall didn't have a dinner engagement with you last night.

00:51:52.020 --> 00:51:52.830
No, he did not.

00:51:53.770 --> 00:51:54.890
You've heard from him lately, though.

00:51:55.330 --> 00:51:57.200
I received the letter which you have there.

00:51:59.040 --> 00:51:59.560
Dear Bert,

00:52:00.190 --> 00:52:04.590
Enclosed find a letter which you will keep with the rest of my stuff for delivery after I'm dead

00:52:04.810 --> 00:52:11.160
It won't be long now, which isn't such a joke as you might think. I won't be seeing you again soon

00:52:11.760 --> 00:52:23.910
Roger you knew a hall pretty well didn't you? Yes. I've been his friend for a number of years

00:52:24.050 --> 00:52:30.000
I'm the executor of his estate whatever it is. Go and get miss Kester for me

00:52:40.080 --> 00:52:42.640
You can tell by the way they're acting they don't think it's a suicide.

00:52:42.640 --> 00:52:45.040
Cliff, it's no use. We can't go on. We've got to tell them.

00:52:45.040 --> 00:52:47.520
Gene, now do as I say. You've got to keep your mouth shut.

00:52:47.520 --> 00:52:50.490
It's our only chance. You don't know the police like I do.

00:52:50.490 --> 00:52:55.480
Come on, Romeo and Juliet. The chief wants to see you. Come on.

00:53:08.440 --> 00:53:12.780
Mr. Howe brought me a letter to you from Mr. Hall.

00:53:12.780 --> 00:53:13.620
- Well, I don't understand.

00:53:13.620 --> 00:53:15.010
Why should he write me a letter?

00:53:15.010 --> 00:53:17.890
- It was to be delivered to you after his death.

00:53:17.890 --> 00:53:27.640
I'd like you to read it.

00:53:27.640 --> 00:53:30.000
Do you mind if I read it

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:31.080
No, go ahead.

00:53:31.080 --> 00:53:46.040
Dear Gene, once upon a time many years ago, I amused you for hours by crawling on all

00:53:46.040 --> 00:53:47.670
fours back.

00:53:47.670 --> 00:53:50.970
Now you know the other afternoon was not our first meeting.

00:53:50.970 --> 00:53:55.140
Small wonder then, I may have appeared to you like some strangely remembered ghost from

00:53:55.140 --> 00:53:56.290
